  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b473bf0cde498904fbfebfc662d072ac, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::GameFinishManager
  objectsToDeliver:
  - {fileID: 0}
  - {fileID: 0}
  - {fileID: 0}
  - {fileID: 0}
  - {fileID: 0}
  objectsDelivered: 000000000001
  missionTexts:
  - Second job is on 12 Victory Street.  Clients had to flee the place. Too scared
    to go back themselves. They just want their things out.  Emotionally valuable
    stuff, so be careful with it. I'll send the list. Don't hang around in there 
    longer than you need to. This one feels different.
  - Because the rules and context of the job have  already been established in the
    House 1 call, this call does not repeat them. Its sole purpose is  to raise the
    stakes and deepen unease before players enter the second house. The tone is 
    noticeably more strained than the first call the dispatcher, who projected control
    and  indifference in House 1, now sounds uncertain.
  - ' The shift in the dispatcher''s composure is  significant: if the person sending
    players into these jobs sounds unsettled, it signals that House  2 is beyond
    even their usual frame of reference. The mention of emotionally valuable items
    also  quietly reintroduces the damage stakes without restating the rules explicitly,'
  - ' and adds a layer of  moral weight; these aren''t just objects, they''re what
    the family chose to risk going back for. '
  missionText: {fileID: 8326172873565854308}
  textindex: 0
  eventSystem: {fileID: 0}
  MissionPanel: {fileID: 8718440401406302139}
  NextButton: {fileID: 2581382657649642567}
  SceneToLoad: House 2
